message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "inner-extremal-rbh: code and data for inner-extremal regular black holes with NEC-satisfying anisotropic sources"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for the paper "Inner-extremal regular black holes with
  NEC-satisfying anisotropic sources: existence, extent, and the absence of a
  classical selection mechanism". Contains the scripts, result files, figures
  and raw logs behind every number reported in the paper.

  A family of regular black holes whose inner horizon is a triple root of the
  metric function exists over a finite range of the core scale and satisfies the
  null energy condition throughout. No local matter source in general relativity
  selects it: between the horizons the geometry is a homogeneous Kantowski-Sachs
  region whose flow preserves phase-space volume identically, so a degenerate
  inner horizon can never be an attractor, and with a velocity-dependent
  transverse pressure it is never asymptotically stable. This release adds that
  theorem, its symbolic proof and numerical controls, the non-spherical analysis,
  and the phase-space area figure.
